{
  "schema": 1,
  "description": "What an activity log entry did, for the Activity screens (docs/activity.md). Input: the entity (table), the action the server logged (create, update, delete, restore) and the before and after rows (only the columns that matter are listed). Output 'change': create is added, delete is deleted, restore is restored; an update is the first that applies of: tasks: completed (status to done), dropped (status to dropped), reopened (status from done or dropped to open), moved (planned_date changed; 'day' is the new date, null for none), renamed (title changed); goals: completed, dropped and reopened the same way, renamed (title changed); areas: archived (archived_at set), unarchived (archived_at cleared), renamed (name changed); tags: renamed; task_steps: checked (done to true), unchecked (done to false), renamed; reminders: handled (state to done or dismissed), snoozed (state to snoozed); habits: archived (archived_at set), unarchived (archived_at cleared), renamed (name changed); habit_checkins: skipped (skipped true), checked (value 1 or more), unchecked (value below 1); habit_pauses: resumed (ends_on set), paused (a create, and otherwise); otherwise edited. 'subject' is the row's title (tasks, task_steps, goals) or name (areas, tags, habits) from 'after', else null.",
